<section class="page-header">
<div class="container">
<p style="margin-bottom:8px;"><a href="/blog/" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.7);font-size:0.9rem;text-decoration:none;">&larr; Back to Blog</a></p>
<h1>Cranberry Festival Vans: Final Call for the 53rd Cranfest</h1>
<p>Five weeks to September 25&ndash;27. What's realistically left in the fleet, the two-minivan fallback, and why the call should happen this week.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section">
<div class="container">
<div style="max-width:800px;margin:0 auto;">
<p>We <a href="warrens-cranberry-festival-van-booking-update-2026.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">said it in July</a>: the vans book up by midsummer. It's now mid-August, the 53rd <strong>Warrens Cranberry Festival</strong> (September 25&ndash;27) is five weeks out, and this is the honest final call for festival transportation.</p>
<p>The festival draws over 100,000 visitors to a village of about 400 people. Parking is the pain point every single year — which is exactly why one vehicle full of people beats six cars hunting for six spots.</p>
<h2>Where availability stands in mid-August</h2>
<p><strong>The 15-passenger van:</strong> festival weekend is its most-requested weekend of the fall, and by now it's either spoken for or close to it. Call for a live answer — cancellations happen, and being the first name on the list costs nothing.</p>
<p><strong>The 7-passenger minivans:</strong> usually the last group vehicles standing at this point, but move-in season and Labor Day are pulling on them too. This week, not next.</p>
<p><strong>Cars and the SUV:</strong> for a group of four making a day trip, an intermediate or full-size car is the low-drama option and rarely sells out this far ahead.</p>
<h2>The two-minivan fallback</h2>
<p>If the big van is gone, don't scrap the group plan. Two <a href="7-passenger-minivan-rental-black-river-falls.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">7-passenger minivans</a> move 14 people for $78/day + $0.10/mile each &mdash; and the split-fleet setup has real upsides: two pickup points for a group scattered between Tomah and Black River Falls, two schedules (early-birds for the cranberry bog tours, late risers for the craft rows), and the same parking lot at the end.</p>
<h2>Vendors: think weekly, not daily</h2>
<p>Selling at the festival? Setup, stock runs, and teardown stretch across most of a week &mdash; and any rental of 7+ days includes <strong>unlimited mileage</strong>. The minivan runs $450/week, the 15-passenger van $750/week. For a crafter hauling a booth from La Crosse or Eau Claire and restocking daily, the weekly van usually beats four stacked daily rentals.</p>
<h2>The short drive is the easy part</h2>
<p>Warrens sits about <strong>25 minutes from our lot</strong> on Highway 54 &mdash; an easy shot down I-94. A festival day trip fits comfortably inside every mileage tier, so the vehicle choice is really about seats and schedule, not miles. We're also the closest van fleet to the festival grounds; renters coming from <a href="/locations/warrens.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">Warrens</a>, Tomah, and Sparta pick up here on the way through.</p>
<p><strong>Call or text 715-396-1466</strong> with your headcount and dates. If the vehicle you want is available, a phone call locks it; if it isn't, we'll tell you straight and set up the best fallback.</p>
<div style="margin-top:48px;">
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-list">
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Can I still get a 15-passenger van for Cranfest 2026?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>Possibly — availability changes daily this close in. Call 715-396-1466 for a live answer, and get on the cancellation list if it's booked.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">What if the big vans are gone?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>Two 7-passenger minivans move 14 people with more scheduling flexibility than one big van. Full-size cars cover smaller day-trip groups.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">How far is Warrens from Black River Falls?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>About 25 minutes down I-94. A festival day trip stays well inside every mileage tier.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Is there a better deal for vendors working all week?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes — rentals of 7+ days include unlimited mileage. Weekly rates: minivan $450, 15-passenger van $750.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
